Kanban helps visualize the work, it is a flexible framework designed for continuous flows..

this works for production support teams because it handles interruptions naturally.. things like
WP incidents, change of priorities, putting out fires, drive-bys etc.

No, you are not supposed to use interrupts or add unplanned work during an active Scrum sprint because it breaks the team's focus and ruins the sprint goal.

in a scrum framework, you are supposed to have two meetings at the end of the sprint

the sprint review  what to build next and what was completed

the sprint retrospective. what went well, what failed and what to fix.


